mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Introduction to Biomedical Informatics is a cross-curricular course integrating biology, medicine and information science. The course will systematically introduce the basic concepts, core theories and cutting-edge technologies of biomedical informatics, covering a variety of aspects such as the diversity of biological data, database fundamentals, data analysis and mining methods, clinical information systems and data models. Students will master the knowledge and analysis methods of biomedical information from basic to cutting-edge, and have the basic ability to analyze and process biomedical data.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
